    docs(gitreins): record evidence files, ref union and the 120s step-budget failure mode (DF-SPECLANG-12)
    
    Follow-up to e2340755 (the previous dispatch of this same task, which already
    landed the config knobs and the runbook for this worktree). This commit adds only
    what I re-verified against the installed tool myself, plus the operator knowledge
    that explains a verdict reading FAIL.
    
    Verified in gitreins 0.21.0 source (pipx venv, site-packages/engine/):
      * persist.py:100 DEFAULT_HISTORY_CONFIG -- enabled/path/storage/max_verdicts
      * persist.py:218-223 config_schema._HISTORY -- the authoritative key set
      * persist.py:261-265 entry dir = <UTC date>/sha256("{task_id}:{evaluated_at}")[:8]
      * persist.py:154 HISTORY_REF = refs/gitreins/history (storage: git target)
      * persist.py:283-309 writes verdict.json + summary.md, and the evidence
        collector's commit.patch / worktree.patch next to them
      * persist.py:951-973 _prune_old drops the OLDEST entries past max_verdicts
        (<= 0 disables), which is what the config comment claims
    
    Doc additions (docs/gitreins-verdicts.md):
      * the two evidence patch files are named -- the entry dir is the audit unit a
        board closeout can quote, not just verdict.json;
      * the ref is shared by every worktree while each checkout keeps its own
        .gitreins/history/ dir, so the ref is the union (measured: three runs on the
        ref for 2026-11-17, one on this checkout's disk);
      * `pipeline.stages[].steps[].timeout` (default 120s) is what turns a completed
        run into `passed: false` / DEGRADED on this repo's full vitest suite -- so a
        DEGRADED verdict is not a persistence failure.
    
    End-to-end proof from this checkout (tier 1 only, no 25-minute judge burned):
      gitreins task start PROBE-DF12 && gitreins task complete PROBE-DF12 --skip-tier2
      -> Overall: PASS, "Verdict saved: 26195795" (that id is the history-ref commit,
         NOT the entry dir), entry dir .gitreins/history/2026-11-17/01e5ab88/ with
         verdict.json + summary.md + commit.patch + worktree.patch, verdict bound to
         commit 3cb333b5 on wt/DF-SPECLANG-12, pass_class tier1-only.
    
    Limits, stated rather than papered over: `--skip-tier2` means no tier-2 judge
    ran, so this record cannot satisfy a judge-gated merge. The unknown-key detector
    was exercised IN-BAND only -- the harness blocks writing a scratch
    .gitreins/config.yaml, so no deliberate-bogus-key arm was run; what was measured
    is the same `gitreins config-validate` invocation warning on six pre-existing
    keys while naming nothing under `history:`. And
    `git ls-remote origin 'refs/gitreins/*'` is empty, so ref-carried evidence is
    per-checkout until pushed explicitly.
    
    Addresses DF-SPECLANG-12.
